1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:04,080
The README's latency numbers are simulated.

2
00:00:04,150 --> 00:00:06,750
So I measured a real voice cascade.

3
00:00:07,110 --> 00:00:13,750
The repo can't call xAI speech, so I wrote a scratch adapter. It is not in the
repo.

4
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:16,200
The repo's own code does the timing.

5
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:22,580
Twenty utterances, each through speech-to-text, the model, and text-to-speech.

6
00:00:22,610 --> 00:00:25,630
Real calls, one provider, one run.

7
00:01:00,290 --> 00:01:07,030
End to end, median two thousand twenty-two milliseconds, p95 two thousand five
hundred eighty-eight.

8
00:01:07,060 --> 00:01:12,180
Speech, model, voice: real. Turn detection: simulated, not counted.

9
00:01:12,270 --> 00:01:15,930
One reply tripped the repo's check. Cost: six cents.

10
00:01:17,070 --> 00:01:21,120
For a client: shadow mode first, then a gated write.

11
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:25,620
Risk: a twenty-turn p95 read as a service level.

12
00:01:25,860 --> 00:01:31,240
ROI: [EST], about twenty-nine hundred currency units a month, gross.

